# Refuse a push that would publish, to the public repository, a history
# unrelated to main or content the publication boundary rejects (#2365).
# Pushes to any other remote pass straight through. The guard reads git's
# ref lines on stdin, so exec it rather than run it in a pipeline.
#
# scripts/install-publication-push-hook.sh, which npm install runs, installs a
# pre-push hook that runs the guard whatever is checked out and then runs this
# file. It sets NG_PUBLICATION_GUARD_RAN to its own process id, which is this
# file's parent's, so the guard runs once. A value inherited from anywhere else
# does not match, and the guard runs.
# See docs/PUBLIC_CORE_BOUNDARY.md § Checked before it is pushed.
[ "${NG_PUBLICATION_GUARD_RAN:-}" = "$PPID" ] && exit 0
exec bash "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/scripts/publication-push-guard.sh" "$@"
